	quests: [
		{
			description: [
				"Identify the threat, choose a retreat route and clear loose hazards before committing. Food, blocks, water, a shield and a bow solve more problems than one extra damage enchantment."
				"Agree whether the goal is loot, rescue, mapping or a boss kill. Different goals require different risks and different points at which to leave."
				"If someone says they are not ready, pause. Multiplayer confidence should be shared, not averaged."
				"Prepare for an encounter by identifying damage types, terrain, escape routes, food, healing, and equipment durability. A spare shield and blocks often matter more than a marginally stronger weapon."
			]
			id: "731E73362B4E623D"
			rewards: [{
				id: "2CB50A6B20A9314D"
				type: "xp"
				xp: 10
			}]
			subtitle: "Preparation is stronger than panic"
			tasks: [{
				id: "5F782CA78E548B0C"
				title: "I read this lesson and tried it in the world"
				type: "checkmark"
			}]
			title: "Win Before the Fight Starts"
			x: 0.0d
			y: 0.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["731E73362B4E623D"]
			description: [
				"Raise a shield for telegraphed attacks, then move. Axes can disable shields, explosions can reach around bad cover, and enemies can trap a player who only walks backward."
				"Fight from stable ground with an escape lane. Doorways and narrow bridges are powerful until a teammate needs to pass through them."
				"Carry a spare shield on long expeditions; durability tends to fail at the least cinematic moment."
				"Prepare for an encounter by identifying damage types, terrain, escape routes, food, healing, and equipment durability. A spare shield and blocks often matter more than a marginally stronger weapon."
			]
			id: "0EA291FB12A81BF8"
			rewards: [{
				id: "087B74DBC0058571"
				type: "xp"
				xp: 10
			}]
			subtitle: "Blocking is positioning, not invincibility"
			tasks: [{
				id: "00BB68B4F1D8CE8A"
				title: "I read this lesson and tried it in the world"
				type: "checkmark"
			}]
			title: "Shield Timing and Space"
			x: 2.0d
			y: -2.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["731E73362B4E623D"]
			description: [
				"A bow is for more than damage. Use range to remove creepers, interrupt ranged mobs and pull one enemy away from a dangerous group."
				"Mark allies before firing into a melee and keep lanes clear. Friendly confusion causes more corpse runs than low arrow damage."
				"Spectral information, terrain and patience can be more valuable than firing as quickly as possible."
				"Use Corpse recovery as a second expedition: mark the death, take replacement food and gear, clear threats, and recover methodically. Do not feed repeated deaths into an unrecovered inventory out of frustration."
			]
			id: "62C5BCF193D3D64F"
			rewards: [{
				id: "12C99AFD59CC4F1C"
				type: "xp"
				xp: 10
			}]
			subtitle: "Create time and choose targets"
			tasks: [{
				id: "360F6B542BD3DDC2"
				title: "I read this lesson and tried it in the world"
				type: "checkmark"
			}]
			title: "Ranged Control"
			x: 2.0d
			y: 0.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["731E73362B4E623D"]
			description: [
				"Bring food with strong saturation and reserve special meals for encounters where their effects matter. Heal before the next room, not after entering it."
				"Use JEI and Enchantment Descriptions to understand effects. Fire Resistance, Slow Falling, Water Breathing and Night Vision can turn environmental threats into manageable routes."
				"Keep emergency supplies in a consistent backpack slot so they remain usable under pressure."
				"Use Corpse recovery as a second expedition: mark the death, take replacement food and gear, clear threats, and recover methodically. Do not feed repeated deaths into an unrecovered inventory out of frustration."
			]
			id: "64E05672B46A93FC"
			rewards: [{
