				title: "I read this lesson and tried it in the world"
				type: "checkmark"
			}]
			title: "Enchanting Without Guesswork"
			x: 4.0d
			y: -1.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["64E05672B46A93FC", "14B4AF82F4F94860"]
			description: [
				"Anvil work accumulates prior-work penalties. Plan the final set, combine smaller books intelligently, and avoid repeatedly repairing valuable gear when Mending is available."
				"Easy Anvils improves the interface but does not make every order equally cheap. Compare the result and cost before confirming."
				"Name important equipment. A named tool is easier to discuss, return and record in a shared armoury."
				"Prepare for an encounter by identifying damage types, terrain, escape routes, food, healing, and equipment durability. A spare shield and blocks often matter more than a marginally stronger weapon."
				"If the expected result does not appear, preserve the failed setup and compare its recipe, tooltip, environment, orientation, required interaction, keybind, and available space with one known-good example. Change one variable at a time until the cause is proven."
			]
			id: "0F5172DEB8AF7C69"
			rewards: [{
				id: "05716473812E6929"
				type: "xp"
				xp: 15
			}]
			subtitle: "Combine deliberately before costs climb"
			tasks: [{
				id: "5CE125A18908A68F"
				title: "I read this lesson and tried it in the world"
				type: "checkmark"
			}]
			title: "Anvil Discipline"
			x: 4.0d
			y: 1.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["14B4AF82F4F94860"]
			description: [
				"Open the Curios interface and learn its slots. Artifacts and Relics may require a specific slot, activation input, charge, cooldown or condition before their effect appears."
				"Test one item at a time in a safe place. Overlapping movement, vision or defensive effects can hide which relic is helping or causing trouble."
				"Build loadouts around a task instead of wearing every rare object because it is rare."
				"Curios adds equipment slots outside normal armour. Open its interface, read each item's slot tooltip, and compare effects in a safe place; an unequipped treasure provides no benefit and a bad combination can obscure its own cause."
			]
			id: "6416430518B427C3"
			rewards: [{
