			title: "The Corpse-Run Protocol"
			x: 6.0d
			y: 0.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["62C5BCF193D3D64F", "64E05672B46A93FC"]
			description: [
				"Prioritise enemies that alter the fight: summoners, ranged attackers, crowd-control effects, explosive mobs and anything blocking retreat."
				"Watch animations, sounds and particles before assuming a modded creature follows vanilla timing. Jade can identify the mod; field observation identifies the rule."
				"Leave neutral or territorial creatures alone when combat provides no useful goal. Not every health bar is a quest invitation."
				"Mowzie's encounters telegraph attacks through animation, sound, and arena behaviour. Spend the first moments observing range and recovery windows instead of trading hits until one health bar disappears."
				"Prepare for an encounter by identifying damage types, terrain, escape routes, food, healing, and equipment durability. A spare shield and blocks often matter more than a marginally stronger weapon."
			]
			id: "69706C072B6ACA07"
			rewards: [{
				id: "353A01E7942253AE"
				type: "xp"
				xp: 15
			}]
			subtitle: "Threat is about behaviour, not health alone"
			tasks: [{
				id: "144BECA2C832D396"
				title: "I read this lesson and tried it in the world"
				type: "checkmark"
			}]
			title: "Read Enemy Roles"
			x: 6.0d
			y: 2.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["6416430518B427C3", "79A388CAEFD02CF8", "69706C072B6ACA07"]
			description: [
				"Call targets, hazards and retreats in short language. One player can hold attention, another control range, another carry recovery supplies, but everyone should understand every role."
				"Do not activate bosses, portals or sealed arenas while teammates are looting or reading. Announce the trigger and count readiness."
				"Share specialised gear when it fits the encounter. The strongest item is wasted if it sits in storage while the group needs its effect."
				"Mowzie's encounters telegraph attacks through animation, sound, and arena behaviour. Spend the first moments observing range and recovery windows instead of trading hits until one health bar disappears."
			]
			id: "003DB0959789CCC3"
